{
  "id": "identidad-copias-mutabilidad",
  "track": "python",
  "order": 10,
  "freq": "always",
  "title": "Classic comparisons: is vs ==, copies, mutability",
  "short": "is, ==, copies",
  "summary": "== compares value (calls __eq__); is compares identity: whether it's the same object in memory.",
  "sections": {
    "definition": "<p><code>==</code> compares value (calls <code>__eq__</code>); <code>is</code> compares identity, that is, whether it's the same object in memory. Mutable: list, dict, set and most objects. Immutable: int, float, str, tuple, frozenset. A <strong>shallow copy</strong> duplicates the container but shares what's inside; a <strong>deep</strong> copy copies everything recursively.</p>\n",
    "analogy": "<p><code>is</code> asks whether it's the same physical cup; <code>==</code> asks whether both cups have the same coffee.</p>\n",
    "problem": "<p>Confusing a reference with a copy produces ghost bugs: you modify one customer's order and another's changes. Using <code>is</code> to compare values sometimes works by chance and fails in production.</p>\n",
    "code:example": "<pre class=\"shiki cerebro\" style=\"background-color:#00000000;color:#cfd3ea\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">import</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> copy</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">pedido </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">=</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> {</span><span style=\"color:#FCD34D\">\"cliente\"</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">: </span><span style=\"color:#FCD34D\">\"Ana\"</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">, </span><span style=\"color:#FCD34D\">\"items\"</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">: [</span><span style=\"color:#FCD34D\">\"cafe\"</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">, </span><span style=\"color:#FCD34D\">\"taza\"</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">]}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">alias </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">=</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> pedido                       </span><span style=\"color:#5F6388\"># misma referencia</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">superficial </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">=</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> pedido.copy()          </span><span style=\"color:#5F6388\"># o copy.copy(pedido), dict(pedido)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">profunda </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">=</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> copy.deepcopy(pedido)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">pedido[</span><span style=\"color:#FCD34D\">\"items\"</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">].append(</span><span style=\"color:#FCD34D\">\"filtro\"</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">superficial[</span><span style=\"color:#FCD34D\">\"items\"</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">]   </span><span style=\"color:#5F6388\"># ['cafe', 'taza', 'filtro']  ¡la lista es compartida!</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">profunda[</span><span style=\"color:#FCD34D\">\"items\"</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">]      </span><span style=\"color:#5F6388\"># ['cafe', 'taza']</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">[1, 2] </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">==</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> [1, 2]       </span><span style=\"color:#5F6388\"># True: compara contenido</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">[1, 2] </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">is</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> [1, 2]       </span><span style=\"color:#5F6388\"># False: son dos objetos distintos</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">if</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> cliente </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">is</span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\"> None</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">:    </span><span style=\"color:#5F6388\"># forma correcta de comparar con None</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">    ...</span></span></code></pre>",
    "bad": "<pre class=\"shiki cerebro\" style=\"background-color:#00000000;color:#cfd3ea\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">if</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> estado </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">==</span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\"> None</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">: ...</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">if</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> nombre </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">is</span><span style=\"color:#FCD34D\"> \"Ana\"</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">: ...</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">tablero </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">=</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> [[0] </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">*</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> 3] </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">*</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> 3</span></span></code></pre><p>== None can be overridden; is with strings depends on interpreter details; the last line creates three references to the same row.</p>\n",
    "good": "<pre class=\"shiki cerebro\" style=\"background-color:#00000000;color:#cfd3ea\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">if</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> estado </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">is</span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\"> None</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">: ...</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">if</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> nombre </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">==</span><span style=\"color:#FCD34D\"> \"Ana\"</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">: ...</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">tablero </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">=</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> [[0] </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">*</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> 3 </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">for</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> _ </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">in</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> range(3)]</span></span></code></pre><p>is only for None, True and False (singletons); a comprehension for independent rows.</p>\n",
    "bridge:typescript": "<p><code>is</code> is similar to <code>===</code> between objects (same reference). But <code>==</code> in Python compares content: <code>[1] == [1]</code> is True, whereas in JS <code>[1] === [1]</code> is false. JS's spread <code>{...obj}</code> is a shallow copy, just like <code>dict.copy()</code>, and <code>structuredClone</code> ≈ <code>copy.deepcopy</code>.</p>\n",
    "interview": "<p>== compares values and is compares identity. I use is only with singletons like None. Lists, dictionaries and sets are mutable; numbers, strings and tuples are immutable, which is why tuples can be dictionary keys. Assigning doesn't copy: it creates another reference. A shallow copy duplicates the container and shares the inner objects; if there are nested structures I'm going to modify, I use deepcopy.</p>\n",
    "myths": "<ul>\n<li><code>a = b = []</code> creates a single list with two names.</li>\n<li><code>[[0] * 3] * 3</code>: changing one row changes all three.</li>\n<li><code>is</code> with small integers (-5 to 256) \"works\" because of CPython's cache and is misleading.</li>\n<li>Tuples are immutable, but if they contain a list, that list can change.</li>\n</ul>\n"
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "type": "choice",
      "prompt": "What does this code print?",
      "items": [
        {
          "q": "What does it print?",
          "code": "<pre class=\"shiki cerebro\" style=\"background-color:#00000000;color:#cfd3ea\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">a </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">=</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> [1, 2]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">b </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">=</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> [1, 2]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">print(a </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">==</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> b, a </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">is</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> b)</span></span></code></pre>",
          "options": [
            "True True",
            "True False",
            "False False",
            "False True"
          ],
          "answer": 1,
          "why": "Same content, different objects."
        },
        {
          "q": "What does it print?",
          "code": "<pre class=\"shiki cerebro\" style=\"background-color:#00000000;color:#cfd3ea\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">m </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">=</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> [[0] </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">*</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> 2] </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">*</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> 2</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">m[0][0] </span><span style=\"color:#7DD3FC\">=</span><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\"> 9</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CFD3EA\">print(m)</span></span></code></pre>",
          "options": [
            "[[9, 0], [0, 0]]",
            "[[9, 0], [9, 0]]",
            "[[9, 9], [0, 0]]",
            "Error"
          ],
          "answer": 1,
          "why": "<code>* 2</code> on the outer list repeats the same reference to the row."
        }
      ]
    },
